# -*- encoding: utf-8 -*-
# Arc: UnionKingdom | Scene: UnionKingdom10

translate pt strings:

    old "Sarah was sitting at her desk."
    new "Sarah estava sentada à sua mesa."

    old "In front of her were a series of books on the subjects of political philosophy."
    new "Diante dela havia uma série de livros sobre filosofia política."

    old "Sarah had read her share, growing up in Castle Reinmeer."
    new "Sarah já havia lido bastante, tendo crescido no Castelo Reinmeer."

    old "Still, she felt wholly unprepared for the question before her."
    new "Ainda assim, ela se sentia totalmente despreparada para a questão que tinha diante de si."

    old "Rosanna had always balanced the interests of the nobility and commonfolk."
    new "Rosanna sempre equilibrara os interesses da nobreza e do povo comum."

    old "It was a balance that had worked well enough over the centuries to maintain a peace."
    new "Era um equilíbrio que havia funcionado bem o suficiente ao longo dos séculos para manter a paz."

    old "Marion's uprising had shattered that fact."
    new "A rebelião de Marion havia destruído esse fato."

    old "The truth was that the nobility was now weaker than it had ever been."
    new "A verdade era que a nobreza agora estava mais fraca do que jamais estivera."

    old "In part, Sarah appreciated that fact."
    new "Em parte, Sarah apreciava esse fato."

    old "Difficult questions, long held off by the entrenched powers, were suddenly up for debate."
    new "Questões difíceis, que por muito tempo foram adiadas pelas forças estabelecidas, de repente se tornaram tema de debate."

    old "The increased social mobility of the commonfolk had motivated many to develop new industries, adding to the prosperity of her nation."
    new "A maior mobilidade social do povo comum havia motivado muitos a desenvolverem novas indústrias, aumentando a prosperidade de sua nação."

    old "Yet..."
    new "No entanto..."

    old "Sarah also knew the dangers of antagonizing the nobility."
    new "Sarah também conhecia os perigos de antagonizar a nobreza."

    old "In defending her country from the Tribes, she had been too short-sighted in considering the interests of the Old Houses."
    new "Ao defender seu país contra as Tribos, ela havia sido míope ao considerar os interesses das Antigas Casas."

    old "In turn, thousands had died in the fighting."
    new "Por sua vez, milhares morreram nos combates."

    old "Sarah did not want to risk such a tragedy again."
    new "Sarah não queria arriscar uma tragédia como aquela novamente."

    old "She began to consider."
    new "Ela começou a refletir."

    old "Support the nobility"
    new "Apoiar a nobreza"

    old "Sarah knew that the best option would be to side with the nobility."
    new "Sarah sabia que a melhor opção seria se aliar à nobreza."

    old "Her country had been nearly torn apart by neglecting them once. She would not make that mistake again."
    new "Seu país quase foi destruído por tê-los negligenciado uma vez. Ela não cometeria esse erro novamente."

    old "And would it not also be better for the common folk, if she could thus prevent more bloodshed?"
    new "E não seria também melhor para o povo comum, se ela pudesse assim evitar mais derramamento de sangue?"

    old "Whichever would come to pass, she would have to make certain that the new political decree would favor the nobles."
    new "Independentemente do que acontecesse, ela teria que garantir que o novo decreto político favorecesse os nobres."

    old "Support the commoners"
    new "Apoie o povo"

    old "Sarah knew in her heart that could be loyal to only the common folk."
    new "Sarah sabia, no fundo do coração, que só poderia ser leal ao povo comum."

    old "They were the true heart of her nation. The people that she was tasking with ruling."
    new "Eles eram o verdadeiro coração de sua nação. O povo que ela tinha a tarefa de governar."

    old "It was more than simply a desire. It was her divine obligation."
    new "Era mais do que um simples desejo. Era sua obrigação divina."

    old "Just as it had once been her Father's task."
    new "Assim como antes fora tarefa de seu Pai."

    old "Whichever would come to pass, she would have to make certain that the new political decree would favor the commoners."
    new "Independentemente do que acontecesse, ela teria de garantir que o novo decreto político favorecesse o povo comum."
